"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Rich in Branch Chain Amino Acids"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"The two most common forms of whey powder are \"isolates\" and \"concentrates\" and the type you choose makes the difference between an average supplement\nand a superior one. Those in the industry understand that isolates are the superior protein. Whey concentrates contain less protein and more ingredients that are not desirable, like lactose and fat.The cleaner profile in isolates are more conducive for adding muscle and losing weight. Not all isolates are the same. Please take heed to other isolates on the market loaded with artificial sweeteners, such as sucrolose."},{"type":"Precautions re: Allergies","notes":"Allergen Information: Contains Milk and Soy (Lecithin) Ingredients."},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"Lactose Free, Gluten Free"},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"No Artificial Flavorings"},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"No Artificial Sweeteners"},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"No Growth Hormones"},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"Zero Carb"},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"Zero Fat"},{"type":"FDA Statement of Identity","notes":"DIETARY SUPPLEMENT FOR EVERYBODY"}],"claims":[{"langualCode":"P0065","langualCodeDescription":"Nutrient "},{"langualCode":"P0115","langualCodeDescription":"All Other"}],"events":[{"date":"2011-11-25","type":"Date entered into DSLD"}],"userGroups":[{"dailyValueTargetGroupName":"Adults and children 4 or more years of age","langualCode":"P0250","langualCodeDescription":"Adults and Children 4 years and above"}],"ingredientRows":[{"order":1,"ingredientId":284519,"description":null,"notes":null,"quantity":[{"servingSizeOrder":1,"servingSizeQuantity":1,"operator":"=","quantity":103,"unit":"{Calories}","dailyValueTargetGroup":[],"servingSizeUnit":"Ounce(s)"}],"nestedRows":